  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Quad Vaccine Partnership - Southeast Asia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Quad Vaccine Partnership coordinated the efforts of Australia, India, Japan and the US to deliver more than 400 million safe and effective COVID-19 vaccine doses to Indo-Pacific countries. Support through the Quad Vaccine Partnership also included assistance for vaccine manufacturing, technical assistance to national medicines regulatory agencies and ministries of health, and the provision of consumables and cold-chain infrastructure, either directly or through multilateral channels including COVAX. All reporting on this initiative was undertaken jointly with INN668 Vaccine Access Health Security Initiative.</narrative>
  </description>
